.TH SHARDPOSTCTL-AUTH 1 "2026-10-01" "ShardPost 0.41.0" "ShardPost Manual"
.SH NAME
shardpostctl-auth \- flush the auth cache of every server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B shardpostctl auth flush
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RI [ account ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Every server keeps the logins and lookups Nauthilus answered for a
short time (the auth cache,
.IR auth.cache.ttl ,
30 seconds by default, and
.I auth.cache.lookup_ttl
for lookups). A change in LDAP \(em a locked account, a removed alias, a
new quota, a changed display name \(em reaches ShardPost only when the
entry ends.
.B auth flush
drops the entries at once.
.PP
With an
.I account
it drops every entry whose login name, lookup name or canonical account
is that name, compared without regard to case: the account itself, an
alias or an address all work. Without one it drops every entry.
.PP
The server that answers flushes its own cache before it answers and
records the flush in the cluster's flush log. The other servers apply it
when they are notified and at the latest on their next poll, 60 seconds
later; the command does not wait for them. The flush reaches neither the
Director's routing cache (up to 30 seconds) nor the cache of Nauthilus
itself, which needs its own flush for a change that has to take effect
at once.
.PP
A server without an auth cache (the static backend, or
.I auth.cache.ttl
0) answers that nothing was cached.
.PP
Role:
.BR repair .
The flush is written to the audit log.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the answer as JSON:
.I account
(the name in lower case, or
.B *
for every entry) and
.I cached
(whether the server has an auth cache).
.SH EXAMPLES
An account was locked in LDAP and has to be locked out now (flush
Nauthilus' cache as well):
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl auth flush user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
An alias was removed; LMTP should stop accepting it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl auth flush alias@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
An account moves to another shard: flush it on the source and on the
target shard, then hold the account for at least
.I lookup_ttl
plus the Director's 30 seconds before pinning it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
kubectl -n shardpost exec deploy/shardpost-server -c server -- \\
    shardpostctl auth flush user@example.org
.RE
.fi
.PP
Something looks stale and nobody knows what: flush everything.
.PP
.nf
.RS
shardpostctl auth flush
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Flushed on this server and recorded for the others (or nothing to flush
on a server without an auth cache).
.TP
.B 64
Wrong usage.
.TP
.B 75
This server was flushed, but the flush could not be recorded for the
other servers, or the server could not be reached. Try again.
.TP
.B 77
The caller lacks the role
.BR repair .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shardpostctl (1),
.BR shardpostctl-account (1)
.PP
The auth cache is described in
.I docs/configuration.md
(section auth), what each change costs until it takes effect in
.IR docs/operations/README.md .
